      "HOOK: A significant proportion of acquisitions in Sub-Saharan Africa undergo a post-closing price adjustment. The main cause: incomplete due diligence. In the OHADA zone, the risk is structural — incomplete land registries, informal governance, accounting practices not compliant with SYSCOHADA. A poorly conducted DD turns an opportunity into a loss of several million euros.",

