      "CRITICAL RISKS \u2014 The 7 errors that block or delay licensing files\n\n1. Insufficient or not fully paid-up share capital: The BCEAO and COBAC verify full capital payment before any review. Unpaid capital = immediate file rejection.\n\n2. Non-credible business plan: Unrealistic projections, absence of WCR modeling, growth assumptions without demand justification. Regulators analyze economic viability with the same rigor as an investor.\n\n3. Directors without proven banking or microfinance experience: The CEO must justify at least 5 years of experience in the financial sector. A CEO without this experience = unfavorable opinion from the UMOA Banking Commission or COBAC.\n\n4. Absence of compliant AML/CFT policy: Anti-money laundering compliance is an absolute requirement. The policy must comply with UEMOA Directive No. 02/2015 (UEMOA) or CEMAC Regulation No. 01/16/CEMAC/UMAC/CM of 11 April 2016 (CEMAC), which abrogated Regulation No. 01/03 of 2003. A generic policy copied from the internet = rejection.\n\n5. Inadequate IT system: Absence of transaction traceability, inability to produce prudential statements automatically, insufficient data security.\n\n6. Non-compliant premises: Absence of safe, alarm, or secure access. Premises must be suitable for public deposit collection.\n\n7. Articles of association not compliant with AUSCGIE: Absence of share transfer clauses, board composition, or preemption rights.\n\nImpact: each error can delay the file by 3 to 6 months. A rejected file must be entirely remade.",

