      "HOOK: In 2024, the average amount raised by an African SME in Series A was 3.2M USD (Source: AVCA, African Private Capital Activity Report 2024). Yet, a majority of companies approaching institutional investors are rejected at first screening. The main cause: an unstructured investment file, insufficient governance, and unjustified valuation.",

